1
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:10,620
One floor tile is broken, and a builder needs a new one.

2
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:13,620
The new tile must fit the gap exactly.

3
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:17,080
A tile is the same shape as the old one, but bigger.

4
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:17,880
Will it fit?

5
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:21,070
Pause the video and decide.

6
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:21,270
No.

7
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:26,450
To fit the gap, the tile must be the same shape, and also the same size.

8
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,030
It can be turned round or flipped over, and it will still fit.

9
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:32,910
Remember how we name angles.

10
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:36,070
Angle ABC is the angle at B, the middle letter.

11
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,900
It is between the lines BA and BC.

12
00:00:38,950 --> 00:00:43,970
Two shapes are congruent if they are exactly the same shape and the same size.

13
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:46,930
One fits exactly on top of the other.

14
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:49,820
You may need to turn it, or flip it over.

15
00:00:49,870 --> 00:00:55,380
This second triangle is turned, but its sides are still 3, 4 and 5 centimetres.

16
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,900
The triangles are congruent.

17
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:03,380
Shapes that are the same shape, but a different size, are not congruent.

18
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:04,070
Your turn.

19
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:08,690
A shape and its mirror image: are they congruent, or not congruent?

20
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:11,950
Pause the video and decide.

21
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,250
They are congruent.

22
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:19,030
A reflection flips the shape, but it does not change any length or any angle.

23
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:26,400
In congruent shapes, the matching parts are called corresponding sides and corresponding angles.

24
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:29,010
We write the letters in matching order.

25
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:35,790
If triangle ABC is congruent to triangle XYZ, then A matches X, B matches Y, and C matches Z.

26
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:38,770
Corresponding sides are equal: AB equals XY.

27
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:43,050
Corresponding angles are equal: angle B equals angle Y.

28
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:43,780
Your turn.

29
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:46,830
Triangle KLM is congruent to triangle RST.

30
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,430
Angle L is 72 degrees.

31
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,590
What is angle S?

32
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:52,950
Pause the video and try it.

33
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,890
L and S are both the second letter, so they are corresponding angles.

34
00:01:57,940 --> 00:02:00,010
Angle S is 72 degrees.

35
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,320
Here is the method.

36
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:07,300
Step 1: check that the shapes are the same type, with the same number of sides.

37
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:10,980
Step 2: match up the corresponding sides and angles.

38
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:14,080
Turn or flip the shape in your head.

39
00:02:14,130 --> 00:02:20,030
Step 3: if every matching side and angle is equal, the shapes are congruent.

40
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:25,620
If the shape is the same but the size is different, they are not congruent.

41
00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:29,700
Quadrilateral ABCD is congruent to quadrilateral EFGH.

42
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:34,840
AB is 7 centimetres, BC is 5 centimetres, and EH is 4.5 centimetres.

43
00:02:34,890 --> 00:02:36,530
Find FG and AD.

44
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:38,520
F matches B, and G matches C.

45
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:41,820
So FG equals BC, which is 5 centimetres.

46
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,870
A matches E, and D matches H.

47
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:47,380
So AD equals EH, which is 4.5 centimetres.

48
00:02:47,430 --> 00:02:50,620
Triangle PQR is congruent to triangle UVW.

49
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:54,320
Angle P is 45 degrees and angle Q is 75 degrees.

50
00:02:54,370 --> 00:02:55,870
Find angle W.

51
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:58,670
W is the third letter, so it matches R.

52
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,030
First find angle R.

53
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:03,950
The angles in a triangle add up to 180 degrees.

54
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,680
180 minus 45 minus 75 is 60.

55
00:03:06,730 --> 00:03:12,300
Angle R is 60 degrees, so angle W is 60 degrees too.

56
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:15,450
Triangle A has sides 5, 12 and 13.

57
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,590
Triangle B has sides 12, 13 and 5.

58
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:21,830
Triangle C has sides 10, 24 and 26.

59
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,230
Which are congruent?

60
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,380
A and B have the same 3 lengths.

61
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:30,430
The order does not matter, so A and B are congruent.

62
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,810
Every side of C is 2 times as long.

63
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,990
C is the same shape, but bigger.

64
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:37,860
It is not congruent to the others.

65
00:03:37,910 --> 00:03:43,150
Two equilateral triangles have sides of 3 centimetres and 5 centimetres.

66
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,540
Are they congruent?

67
00:03:44,590 --> 00:03:46,230
Here is Noor's working.

68
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,840
Which line goes wrong first?

69
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:49,950
Line 2 is wrong.

70
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,370
Congruent needs the same shape and the same size.

71
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:56,990
These triangles have different side lengths.

72
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,610
So they are not congruent.

73
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:02,120
Factories depend on congruent shapes.

74
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:09,120
Every screen protector for one model of phone is congruent, so it fits any phone of that model.

75
00:04:09,170 --> 00:04:12,440
A copy of a key must be congruent to the original.

76
00:04:12,490 --> 00:04:16,780
If it is even slightly different, the lock will not open.

77
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:22,650
And in a jigsaw, each piece fits only one hole: the hole that is congruent to it.

78
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:23,980
One last question.

79
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:25,750
One rectangle is 4 by 6.

80
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,080
Another is 6 by 4.

81
00:04:27,130 --> 00:04:29,810
Are they congruent, or not congruent?

82
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:33,210
Pause the video and answer.

83
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:34,500
They are congruent.

84
00:04:34,550 --> 00:04:39,200
The second rectangle is the first one, turned a quarter turn.

85
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:44,230
To remember: congruent shapes are identical in shape and in size.

86
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,890
They may be turned or flipped.

87
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:52,040
Corresponding sides are equal, and corresponding angles are equal.

88
00:04:52,090 --> 00:04:56,520
Write the letters of congruent shapes in matching order.

89
00:04:56,570 --> 00:05:01,590
Great work! Now practise lesson 8.3 on Camday.
